{"title":"Group theory","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Group theory</b> is the area of mathematics which deals directly with the study of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Group\" title=\"Group\">groups</a>.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Group_theory&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Topics_and_results_in_group_theory\">Topics and results in group theory</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Group_theory&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Topics and results in group theory\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Coset\" title=\"Coset\">Cosets</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Normal_subgroup\" title=\"Normal subgroup\">Normal subgroups</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Lagrange%27s_Theorem\" title=\"Lagrange&#39;s Theorem\">Lagrange's Theorem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Jordan-H%C3%B6lder_Theorem\" title=\"Jordan-Hölder Theorem\">Jordan-Hölder Theorem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Orbit\" title=\"Orbit\">Orbit</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Stabilizer\" title=\"Stabilizer\">Stabilizer</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sylow_Theorems\" title=\"Sylow Theorems\">Sylow Theorems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Free_group\" title=\"Free group\">Free groups</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Free_abelian_group&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Free abelian group (page does not exist)\">Free abelian groups</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018085959\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nCompli